    "title": "Boulder County sees biggest snowfall of the season - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Abigail Ankeney Celia Frazier ,\n1 days ago Wednesday’s snowstorm flung flakes across Boulder County, with Boulder and Longmont seeing their first substantial snow accumulations of the winter season. By the end of the day, snow accumulation across the county ranged from 5.5 inches to 11 inches, with little accumulation expected into the evening. Here’s what parts of the county received as of late Wednesday afternoon and what residents can expect for the rest of the week. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 10",
